// DAX measures for the Ontario demand forecast report.
//
// These expect the table to be called Forecast (see power_query.m).
// Power BI takes one measure at a time: select the Forecast table, click
// "New measure", paste one block, press Enter, then set the format noted above it.
//
// abs_pct_error and baseline_abs_pct_error are stored as fractions (0.034 = 3.4%),
// so the percentage measures only need the Percentage format, not a x100.


// ---- Headline measures ------------------------------------------------------

// The model's average error (MAPE): on average, how far off each hourly
// prediction is, as a share of the real demand.
// Format: Percentage, 2 decimals.
Avg Abs Error % = AVERAGE ( Forecast[abs_pct_error] )

// The same thing for the baseline guess, "same hour yesterday".
// Format: Percentage, 2 decimals.
Baseline Avg Abs Error % = AVERAGE ( Forecast[baseline_abs_pct_error] )

// How much smaller the model's average % error is than the baseline's.
// DIVIDE returns blank instead of an error if the baseline is 0 or missing.
// Format: Percentage, 2 decimals.
Improvement vs Baseline % =
DIVIDE (
    [Baseline Avg Abs Error %] - [Avg Abs Error %],
    [Baseline Avg Abs Error %]
)

// The hour of day (0-23, hour beginning, EST) with the largest average % error.
// Builds a 24-row table of average error per hour, keeps the worst row, and
// returns its hour. Ties go to the earlier hour. Respects slicers, so it shows
// the worst hour for whatever dates are selected.
// Format: Whole number.
Peak-Error Hour =
VAR ErrorByHour =
    ADDCOLUMNS ( VALUES ( Forecast[hour] ), "@AvgError", [Avg Abs Error %] )
VAR Worst =
    TOPN ( 1, ErrorByHour, [@AvgError], DESC, Forecast[hour], ASC )
RETURN
    MAXX ( Worst, Forecast[hour] )


// ---- Megawatt versions (these match the README and the Streamlit dashboard) --

// Average miss in MW (MAE).
// Format: Whole number, thousands separator.
Avg Miss MW = AVERAGE ( Forecast[abs_error_mw] )

// Average miss in MW for the baseline.
// Format: Whole number, thousands separator.
Baseline Avg Miss MW = AVERAGE ( Forecast[baseline_abs_error_mw] )

// How much smaller the model's average MW miss is than the baseline's. This is
// the README's "23% smaller" figure. It differs from Improvement vs Baseline %
// because a MW miss counts the same at any demand level, while a % miss
// counts for more when demand is low.
// Format: Percentage, 2 decimals.
Improvement vs Baseline (MW) % =
DIVIDE ( [Baseline Avg Miss MW] - [Avg Miss MW], [Baseline Avg Miss MW] )

// Number of hours in the current selection.
// Format: Whole number, thousands separator.
Hours Tested = COUNTROWS ( Forecast )


// ---- For the line chart -----------------------------------------------------

// AVERAGE rather than SUM, so the lines still read in MW if the chart is ever
// rolled up from hours to days or months.
// Format: Whole number, thousands separator.
Actual MW = AVERAGE ( Forecast[actual_mw] )

Predicted MW = AVERAGE ( Forecast[predicted_mw] )
